# Offline Support Rules

Define server behavior for sync-capable clients.

## Requirements
- Offline-capable mutations must use idempotency and deterministic conflict handling.
- Endpoints exposed to offline clients should support incremental sync metadata.
- Sync metadata (`updated_since`, version/etag fields) must use `human_friendly_id` for record identity.
- After successful reconciliation, persisted mutations must still emit scoped realtime events per `websockets.mdc`.
- Account authentication, session issuance/revocation, entitlement or role changes, consent withdrawal, connector scope changes, export approval/download authorization, and security-sensitive approvals are online-only.
- Conflict responses must identify the conflicting record and latest version metadata.
- Server logic must not assume the client clock is authoritative.

